All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: made role comparison case-insensitive by lowercasing both `required` and each role in `user_roles` (`src/auth.py:9`).
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` so that being either an admin *or* the owner grants access (`src/auth.py:14`).

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: replaced mutable default argument `{}` with `None` + `dict(initial)` copy to prevent shared state between instances (`src/inventory.py:12`).
- `add`: changed from assignment (`= qty`) to accumulation (`+= qty`) so repeated calls add up (`src/inventory.py:16`).
- `reserve`: changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed (`src/inventory.py:24`).
- `release`: added a guard that raises `ValueError` when releasing more than is currently reserved (`src/inventory.py:30`).

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: appended `char.lower()` instead of raw `char`, and replaced the single `replace("--", "-")` with a loop that fully collapses any run of repeated hyphens (`src/text_utils.py:17-22`).
- `truncate`: shortened the kept text slice to `max_len - len(suffix)` so the final string length including the suffix respects the limit (`src/text_utils.py:33`).
